  "description": "Ten stanza-mapped, checksum-pinned native landscape candidates for unapproved D049 reference comparison; S001 v006 is retained as the least-visible disclosed deviation after three authorized attempts, S003 v013 is retained after two failed forehead-fleck edits, and S010 v018 repairs the raised rear foot.",
  "review_notice": "Unapproved landscape candidates for reference comparison only. A fresh all-ten independent exact-checksum review is pending against this final plan. S001 v006 remains the least-visible version after three authorized attempts: five clear toe forms plus a 5–6 px toe-like nub near (1143,873); round-g called it a sixth digit, while round-h passed it at full frame. S003 v013 remains selected because two authorized v014/v015 forehead edits retained the dark 2–3 px fleck near (878,234); both edits changed more than 1.54 million pixel coordinates outside the target area, so the more faithful v013 is retained with the visible fleck disclosed. S010 v018 repairs the raised rear foot from two to five distinct toe forms. Compared with v017, 1,570,839 pixel coordinates changed (1,533,532 outside and 37,307 inside the 220x170 target-foot box); composition remains the same. S010 skin-only medians are Krishna B-R 72/80, Balarama R-B 128 and gopa R-B 122/128/125; human skin reads warm brown and samples are 2–8 above the approximate <120 guide. S004 v006 repairs the open hand to thumb plus four fingers; a gopika cheek sample is R-B 124, four above the approximate <120 guide but visually brown. Photos 001, 003, 004 and 006 are mismatches or unresolved; photos 002 and 005 are broad context only; 007 and 008 are thematic matches; 009 is river context and its unidentified woman is excluded; 010 supports calf tending but its calves are not distinct. No captions are supplied: numbered source commentary is attributed commentary, not a photo caption. Canonical Sanskrit and IAST remain in content/daskams/d049.json; no vetted English verse translation is supplied. Publishing does not approve artwork; portraits remain paused.",
